nadian woman in Canada last week. Being with her is fun, energizing, and makes him feel alive, offering a nice change after dealing with health issues.\n  - spark: Evan felt a spark inside when he saw the woman from Canada, which made him feel like time stopped and that it was so right.\n  - Evan: Evan is motivated by adventure on interesting hikes. Last week, he went on a trip to Canada and met an incredible Canadian woman who makes him feel alive.\n  - Sam: Sam congratulated Evan, asked if a woman mentioned was from Canada, and commented that art is amazing at expressing emotions.\n  - Sam: Sam congratulated Evan on his relationship and asked if he believes in love at first sight after learning Evan was in love with the woman from Canada at first sight.\n  - Evan: Evan married his partner last week. Evan was asked by Sam if his spouse is the woman from Canada. Evan had previously mentioned enjoying books, painting, driving, and hiking.\n  - Sam: Sam greeted Evan, congratulated him, asked about a woman from Canada, and jokingly suggested putting a GPS sensor on Evan's keys.\n  - Sam: Sam greeted Evan, congratulated him on getting married last week, and asked if his spouse was the woman from Canada.\n  - Evan: Evan told his extended family about his marriage and plans to try poutine in Canada next month. He told Sam he had too much to drink last night and did something regrettable involving roses.\n  - innermost thoughts and feelings: Evan describes needing an outlet to express innermost thoughts and feelings to figure things out and make sense of them.\n  - Canada: Evan and his partner are going to Canada next month for their honeymoon to explore snowy landscapes. Sam mentioned something is a Canadian thing.\n  - Evan and partner's bond: Evan told their extended family about their marriage, receiving love and support. Evan feels lucky to have found someone who gets them, strengthening their bond.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":1457,"context_chars":5750,"retrieval