 bigger picture.\n\n2. **Embrace Small Steps**: They would encourage taking small, manageable steps forward, as Evan has suggested to Sam when feeling overwhelmed. This approach can help build confidence and momentum.\n\n3. **Appreciate the Little Things**: Both Evan and Sam recognize the value of appreciating small moments in life. They would advise others to find joy in everyday experiences, which can provide comfort during tough times.\n\n4. **Seek Support**: They would stress the importance of having someone to talk to, as both have supported each other through personal challenges. Reaching out for help can make a significant difference.\n\n5. **Stay Open to New Experiences**: Evan has encouraged Sam to try new things and step out of his comfort zone. They would suggest that embracing new opportunities can lead to unexpected growth and happiness.\n\n6. **Focus on Health and Well-being**: Given their discussions about health, they would likely advise prioritizing physical and mental well-being, including finding enjoyable forms of exercise and maintaining a healthy diet.\n\n7. **Be Patient with Yourself**: They would remind others that transitions take time and that it’s okay to feel challenged. Patience and self-compassion are key during periods of change.\n\n8. **Find Inspiration in Nature**: Sam has found solace in nature, and they would recommend spending time outdoors as a way to recharge and gain perspective.\n\nBy sharing these insights, Evan and Sam would aim to empower others to navigate their challenges with resilience and positivity.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the